    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d648">

                <pb facs="0764" n="679" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg679"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.00/707</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Secretary of War</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Baker</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-08-28"><hi rendition="#italic">August 28,
                        1918</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I am in
                    receipt of a despatch dated July 15, 1918, from the American Legation at Panama
                    City, in which the Legation suggests the advisability of preparing for
                    introduction in the National Assembly of Panama at its session beginning in
                    September, drafts of bills providing for the following objects: (1) The
                    appointment of an American Police Commissioner who shall have full power to
                    control, instruct, and guard the police force of the Republic and (2), The
                    appointment of an American Fiscal Agent who shall have control and charge of the
                    National Treasury.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d648-f1"/></p>
                <p>If you approve these suggestions, I beg to request you to be so good as to
                    instruct Judge Frank Feuille,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d648-f2"/> who is familiar
                    with the laws of Panama, and has ready access to them, to prepare drafts of the
                    legislation suggested, and to submit the drafts to your Department and this
                    Department for their consideration.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A.
                            Adee</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Second Assistant
                        Secretary of State</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d648-f1" n="1" xml:id="d648-f1-content">
                <p>In the despatch, which is not printed, the Minister added: “These two radical
                    reforms, I understand, have long been desired by the Department of State.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d648-f2" n="2" xml:id="d648-f2-content">
                <p>Special attorney for the Panama Canal.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
